================================================================================
  SMB / NFS Enable - OS-specific implementation
================================================================================

ARCHITECTURE
-----------
  sharelib.pl       sharelib_set_smbshare, sharelib_unset_smbshare
  zfslib.pl         prop=sharenfs (NFS), prop=smb_share: -> sharelib
  server.pl         get_smb_conf() -> detects ksmbd or Samba
  $sc               return value of exe("sc") = path to the SMB config file

SMB ENABLE
----------
  Entry point: prop=smb_share: -> sharelib_set_smbshare

  Windows (MSWin):
    New-SmbShare via PowerShell:
      New-SmbShare -Name $name -Path "D:\fs" -fullAccess "$admins" -changeaccess "$users"
    Drive letter: zfs get driveletter Pool/fs or Pool
    Groups: Get-LocalGroup | Select SID (544=Admin, 545=User)
    Note: driveletter='off' or '-' -> message, do it manually in Computer
    Management

  Linux (ksmbd or Samba):
    get_smb_conf() priority: see the "SC/ON CONSISTENCY" section below
    (cs_26.07.02 -- priority is now $smb-dependent, no longer a plain
    file-existence check).
    ksmbd:  systemctl restart ksmbd
    Samba:  systemctl restart smbd   (NOT "samba" -- that is not a valid
            systemd unit name on Debian/Ubuntu/Proxmox, see below)
    TrueNAS: midclt call service.restart cifs
    Config: rcmd:writefile::/etc/samba/smb.conf::[share]\npath=...

  FreeBSD:
    Samba: service samba_server restart
    Config: smb4.conf in /usr/local/etc/

  Illumos/OmniOS:
    zfs set sharesmb=name=$name[,abe=true] $zfs
    no smb.conf -- OS-native SMB
    svcadm restart smb/server

  Oracle Solaris 11:
    zfs set share=name=$name,path=/fs,prot=smb[,guestok=true] $zfs
    zfs set sharesmb=on $zfs
    svcadm restart smb/server

NFS ENABLE
----------
  Entry point: prop=sharenfs -> zfslib.pl

  Illumos/OmniOS ("solaris;illumos" in the on-string):
    /Solaris/i matches -> Solaris branch
    /Solaris.11/ does NOT match -> else branch:
      zfs set sharenfs=$text $zfs   (on/off or options)
    CORRECT: no share= command (Oracle Solaris 11 only)

  Oracle Solaris 11:
    zfs set share=name=NFS-$ds,path=/$zfs,prot=nfs[,options] $zfs
    zfs set sharenfs=on $zfs

  FreeBSD:
    edit /etc/exports (rcmd:writefile)
    service nfsd restart 2>/dev/null || service nfs restart

  Linux (Proxmox, Debian, ...):
    edit /etc/exports (rcmd:writefile)
    systemctl enable nfs-kernel-server || systemctl enable nfs-server
    systemctl restart nfs-kernel-server || systemctl restart nfs-server

KSMBD DETECTION
---------------
  server.pl get_smb_conf() (BEFORE cs_26.07.02, only still relevant when
  $smb was not set beforehand, e.g. the BSD branch):
    1. -f /etc/ksmbd/ksmbd.conf  -> return path (ksmbd has PRIORITY due to RDMA)
    2. find /etc/samba smb.conf  -> Linux Samba
    3. find /usr smb.conf        -> TrueNAS
    4. find /usr/local smb4.conf -> FreeBSD
    5. find /opt smb.conf        -> OmniOS Samba
  sharelib.pl: samba_conf =~/ksmbd/ -> samba_restart = systemctl restart ksmbd

================================================================================
  SC/ON CONSISTENCY -- systemd active-service detection (cs_26.07.02)
================================================================================

  BUG FOUND THIS SESSION (real host: proxmox_2, Proxmox/Debian, ksmbd kernel
  module loaded):
    - "on" reported smb="ksmbd" (kernel module loaded, via lsmod check)
    - "sc" (get_smb_conf()) returned /etc/samba/smb.conf anyway, because
      /etc/ksmbd/ksmbd.conf did not exist yet -- get_smb_conf() only
      preferred ksmbd.conf if the FILE already existed, independent of what
      "on" reported.
    - Every smb_share write therefore landed in Samba's config, which
      nothing was reading.
    - Additionally, the restart command used "systemctl restart samba" --
      not a valid systemd unit name on Debian/Ubuntu/Proxmox (that's an
      Illumos/Solaris SMF naming convention; the actual unit is "smbd").
      The restart therefore always failed silently, so even writes to the
      correct file (smb.conf) would never have taken effect.
    - It further turned out Samba's daemon package wasn't even installed on
      that host at all (`systemctl status smbd` -> "Unit smbd.service could
      not be found.") -- confirmed via `ss -tlnp | grep :445` returning
      nothing (no SMB listener at all).

  FIX (server.pl, my_os() Linux branch + get_smb_conf()):
    $smb is now determined via `systemctl is-active smbd`/`ksmbd`
    (authoritative -- reflects what's ACTUALLY serving, not just installed
    or kernel-module-loaded) BEFORE get_smb_conf() runs. The old ps/lsmod
    heuristic is kept as a fallback only for non-systemd hosts or when
    systemctl reports nothing active yet.
    get_smb_conf() now checks $smb first: if $smb eq "ksmbd", it always
    returns /etc/ksmbd/ksmbd.conf -- even if the file doesn't exist on disk
    yet -- instead of silently falling through to the Samba file-existence
    search. This guarantees "sc" and "on" can never disagree again for any
    caller that determines $smb before calling get_smb_conf() (currently:
    the Linux branch; BSD/other branches don't set $smb first, so
    get_smb_conf() falls through to the original file-existence logic for
    them, unchanged).

  FIX (modifier.pl full_smb_share(), same session, frontend side):
    Independently also checks $current{'on'}/$in{'on'} =~ /ksmbd/i and
    hardcodes /etc/ksmbd/ksmbd.conf + "systemctl restart ksmbd" when true,
    creating the file if missing -- this predates the server.pl fix above
    and is now technically redundant with it, but left in place as a
    harmless defense-in-depth check (also useful if a member is running an
    older server.pl that hasn't received this fix yet). Also fixed:
    "systemctl restart samba" -> "systemctl restart smbd" for the
    non-ksmbd/non-BSD branch, and _is_zfs_error() broadened to also catch
    systemd's "Failed to restart ..."/"...could not be found." wording
    (previously silently treated as success -- neither starts with
    "error"/"cannot "/"timeout").

