  TODO (not yet implemented -- Gea request 2026.07.29): SMB share
  enable should verify/add a required PAM line on Solaris/illumos
================================================================================

  When enabling an SMB share on Solaris or illumos, the PAM config must
  contain a line enabling pam_smb_passwd.so.1, or SMB auth fails. Check
  should run as part of the SMB-share-enable flow (modifier.pl
  full_smb_share() or sharelib.pl, wherever the Solaris/illumos SMB
  enable branch lives) and append the line if missing:

  Solaris: /etc/pam.d/other must contain (append at end if missing):
      password required   pam_smb_passwd.so.1 nowarn

  Illumos: /etc/pam.conf must contain (append at end if missing):
      other   password required   pam_smb_passwd.so.1 nowarn

  Not yet implemented -- this is a reminder/spec only. Next session:
  find the Solaris/illumos SMB-enable code path, add a check (read the
  file via &exe("cat ...") through the now-fixed server.pl cat
  fast-path, or via socket "on"-based OS branch already used elsewhere)
  and append the line via the existing rcmd:writefile mechanism if the
  exact line isn't already present. Idempotent -- must not duplicate
  the line on repeated SMB-enable calls.
